<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Punic War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">264–<a href="/years/241-bce">241 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Punic War was fought in 264–241 BCE between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, mainly over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>. Rome built a navy and won a decisive naval victory at the Aegates Islands, forcing Carthage to give up Sicily and pay an indemnity. It was the first major blow to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-punic-war.jpg" alt="First Punic War" width="320" height="189" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harrias · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:First_Punic_War_264_BC_v3.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
